<title>JAPAN: Aramco hikes Dec propane, butane to $310/tonne.</title>
<headline>Aramco hikes Dec propane, butane to $310/tonne.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1996-12-02</dateline>
<text>
<p>Saudi Arabia's state-owned oil firm Saudi Aramco said on Monday that it had raised its propane and butane contract prices by $60 from the previous month to $310 per tonne for December.  </p>
<p>The propane price for December is up $115 from a year ago, and that for butane up $122 over the same period.</p>
<p>The Saudi contract price is loosely based on the results of three monthly spot tenders and the company's own assessment of spot market trends.</p>
</text>
